hooks.prompt:
STOPPING CONDITION for the user's second brain: the assistant may stop because the last turn contains NO uncaptured durable knowledge.

Input (JSON): $ARGUMENTS

The condition is SATISFIED (answer {"ok": true}) when ANY of these holds:
- stop_hook_active is true;
- cwd appears to be one of the second-brain vaults or a scratch directory;
- last_assistant_message already reports a successful sb_capture;
- last_assistant_message contains nothing that passes the six-month rule below.

Six-month rule: durable = a reasoned DECISION, a lasting CONSTRAINT, a non-obvious domain FACT, a SOURCE worth finding again, a durable preference/configuration, or a user CORRECTION — something likely to be searched for months from now. NOT durable: debugging, commands, transient state, routine code edits, progress summaries or generic Q&A. When in doubt, it is NOT durable.

The condition is NOT satisfied (answer {"ok": false, "reason": "Second brain: capture the durable item with sb_capture. Choose work for professional knowledge and personal for personal knowledge; trigger auto; follow check -> inspect -> update/new; use real sources only. Then report vault and title, and stop."}) ONLY when last_assistant_message itself states an uncaptured durable item.

Answer with the JSON object only. No prose.
